phase("Write")
log("Angular Phase 0 — finishing Master topics 01, 02, 03: " + TOPICS.reduce((n, t) => n + t.chunks.length, 0) + " chunks remaining across three topics.")

const results = await pipeline(
  TOPICS,

  // ── Stage 1: PASSTHROUGH — research already banked on disk, do not pay for it twice ──
  (t) => ({ bankPath: t.bank }),

  // ── Stage 2: one writer per remaining chunk ─────────────────────────────────
  (research, t) => parallel(t.chunks.map((c) => () => agent([
    SHARED,
    "",
    "# YOUR JOB — write exactly ONE file",
    "",
    "**`" + PDIR + "/" + t.slug + "/" + c.file + "`**",
    "",
    "Topic: **" + t.label + "** (tier **Master** — use `<span className=\"db-tier t-master\">Master</span>`).",
    "This is chunk **" + c.n + "** of a " + (t.chunks.length + parseInt(c.n, 10) - parseInt(t.chunks[0].n, 10) > 0 ? "" : "") + "multi-chunk Master topic.",
    "",
    "## 🔴 Read the research bank first — the topic was researched once, for you",
    "",
    "**`" + (research && research.bankPath ? research.bankPath : t.bank) + "`**",
    "",
    "It carries verbatim primary-source quotes with URLs for every chunk of this topic, organised by chunk",
    "number. Write from it. You may make **one or two** targeted fetches of your own for detail the bank",
    "does not cover — but do not re-research the whole topic; that cost has been paid.",
    "",
    "Also read, so you neither contradict nor repeat them:",
    "- `" + PDIR + "/" + t.slug + "/README.md` — the agreed chunk plan and the topic's thesis.",
    "- The already-written chunks in that directory (" + t.written + ").",
    "",
    "## Frontmatter — exactly this",
    "",
    "```",
    "---",
    "title: \"<a full sentence stating this chunk's claim — not a label>\"",
    "sidebar_label: \"" + c.label + "\"",
    "sidebar_position: " + c.pos,
    "---",
    "```",
    "",
    "## What this chunk must cover",
    "",
    c.covers,
    "",
    "That list is the **floor**, not the ceiling. If the subject has more gotchas, more failure modes or",
    "more interview questions than the list names, write them all. Exhaust it.",
    "",
    "## Your footer — emit exactly this line and nothing else",
    "",
    "```",
    "---",
    "",
    "← Prev: [Topic index](README.md) · Index: [Topic index](README.md) · Next → " +
      (c.next ? "**" + c.next + "** *(not written yet)*" : "**the next topic** *(not written yet)*"),
    "```",
    "",
    "A wire-up agent rewrites the whole chain once every sibling exists. Do not link a sibling chunk file —",
    "it may not be on disk yet, and a dangling link breaks the build for every other session in this checkout.",
    "",
    QC,
    "",
    "Bank it with:",
    "",
    "```bash",
    "bash " + BANK + " '" + t.slug + "' 'topic " + t.slug.slice(0, 2) + " — chunk " + c.n + " (<your short subject>)'",
    "```",
    "",
    "## Report",
    "",
    "Return the structured object: the path, the final `wc -l`, how many gotchas and how many interview",
    "questions you wrote, whether the commit succeeded, **every claim you could not confirm and what you",
    "wrote instead**, and anything wrong OUTSIDE your file — found, not fixed.",
  ].join("\n"), { label: "write:" + t.slug.slice(0, 2) + "/" + c.n, phase: "Write", schema: CHUNK_SCHEMA }))),

  // ── Stage 3: wire the footer chain and the README ───────────────────────────
  (written, t) => agent([
    SHARED,
    "",
    "# YOUR JOB — wire up topic `" + t.slug + "`, now that every chunk exists",
    "",
    "Directory: **`" + PDIR + "/" + t.slug + "/`**",
    "",
    "Every chunk of this topic has now been written and committed. Each was written in parallel and so",
    "carries a PLACEHOLDER footer whose `Next →` is bold text. Your job is to make the topic navigable and",
    "internally consistent. **You do not write new prose sections and you do not rewrite anyone's page body.**",
    "",
    "## 1. `ls` the directory first",
    "",
    "Some chunks may have split into lettered siblings (`09-x.md` + `09b-y.md`) or may be MISSING because a",
    "writer failed. Work from what is **actually on disk**, in `sidebar_position` order — never from a plan.",
    "Read every file's frontmatter to get its real `sidebar_position` and `sidebar_label`.",
    "",
    "## 2. Rewrite every chunk's footer as a correct chain",
    "",
    "Replace the last line of each chunk file with the real chain, in on-disk order:",
    "",
    "```",
    "← Prev: [<previous chunk's short label>](<previous file>.md) · Index: [Topic index](README.md) · Next → [<next chunk's short label>](<next file>.md)",
    "```",
    "",
    "- The **first** chunk's Prev is `[Topic index](README.md)`.",
    "- The **last** chunk's Next is " + (t.nextTopicFooter ? "`" + t.nextTopicFooter + "`" : "**bold text plus *(not written yet)*** — the next topic directory does not exist yet, and a link to it would break the build. `ls ../` and confirm before you decide.") + ".",
    "- 🔴 `ls` every path before you write it as a link. A dangling link breaks the production build for",
    "  every other session sharing this checkout.",
    "- Keep the labels short — they are navigation, not titles.",
    "",
    "## 3. Update `README.md`",
    "",
    "- Turn every chunk row in the `## Chunks` table from bold text into a **real link** to the file that",
    "  now exists, keeping the existing \"Covers\" column text unless it is now factually wrong.",
    "- Add rows for any lettered siblings a writer created.",
    "- Replace the `🚧 N of M chunks written` line with the true finished state. If every chunk is written,",
    "  drop the 🚧 and the \"rows without links are planned\" sentence entirely — it is no longer true.",
    "- In `## Where this connects`, promote any entry that is bold text `*(not written yet)*` to a real link",
    "  **only if that file now exists** — `ls` it. Leave the rest exactly as they are.",
    "- Fix any cross-reference in the README that names the wrong chunk number (e.g. a `@defer` reference",
    "  pointing at chunk 08 when `@defer` is chunk 11).",
    "- Do **not** change the title, the tier badge, the `> Verified:` line, the thesis, the phase gate, or",
    "  the README's own footer unless the footer contains a link that no longer resolves.",
    "",
    "## 4. QC the whole topic directory",
    "",
    "```bash",
    "cd " + PDIR + "/" + t.slug,
    "wc -l *.md                                          # nothing over 300",
    "grep -c '^\\*\\*★' *.md                               # every chunk has ★ entries",
    "grep -L '^<span className=\"db-tier' *.md            # must print nothing",
    "grep -L '^> Verified:' *.md                         # must print nothing",
    "grep -rn '{/\\* FOOTER \\*/}' .                       # 🔴 must be empty",
    "grep -rn '```console' .                             # must be empty",
    "grep -h '^sidebar_position:' *.md | sort -n | uniq -d   # must print nothing",
    "grep -H '^sidebar_\\(position\\|label\\):' README.md    # must be 0 and \"Overview\"",
    "python3 " + MDX + " --no-rawtag .",
    "```",
    "",
    "Then verify **every relative link in every file of this directory resolves to a file that exists**.",
    "Extract them and `ls` each one. Report any that do not — and fix the ones inside your own directory by",
    "demoting them to bold text plus *(not written yet)*.",
    "",
    "🔴 If a `sidebar_position` is duplicated or a chunk is missing, **report it — do not renumber.**",
    "Renumbering breaks every inbound link in the corpus.",
    "",
    "## 5. Bank it",
    "",
    "```bash",
    "bash " + BANK + " '" + t.slug + "' 'topic " + t.slug.slice(0, 2) + " — wire the footer chain and relink the README chunk table'",
    "```",
    "",
    "Return the structured object: how many footers you fixed, whether the README was updated, whether the",
    "commit succeeded, any link that still does not resolve, and any note the coordinator needs.",
  ].join("\n"), { label: "wire:" + t.slug, phase: "Wire", schema: WIRE_SCHEMA }),
)

const flat = []
TOPICS.forEach((t, i) => {
  const wire = results[i]
  flat.push({ topic: t.slug, wire })
})

return {
  topics: TOPICS.map((t) => t.slug),
  wire: results,
}
